WEBVTT

NOTE Narration is displayed in the caption strip below the video by default.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.667
Check the fictional cost model for one delivery.

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:06.417
All numbers are invented training assumptions.

00:00:06.417 --> 00:00:15.585
The comparison amount is sixty dollars, the tool allocation four dollars and the internal time value thirty dollars per hour.

00:00:15.585 --> 00:00:20.627
Production takes thirty minutes, review twenty, support ten and maintenance ten.

00:00:20.627 --> 00:00:22.461
Add the minutes: seventy.

00:00:22.461 --> 00:00:29.336
Divide by sixty and multiply by thirty to obtain thirty-five dollars of assumed time value.

00:00:29.336 --> 00:00:33.003
Add four to obtain a thirty-nine-dollar modeled subtotal.

00:00:33.003 --> 00:00:37.129
The illustrative remainder is twenty-one dollars before omitted costs.

00:00:37.129 --> 00:00:42.171
The incomplete model counted only production and tools, giving nineteen dollars.

00:00:42.171 --> 00:00:45.380
Review, support and maintenance explain the difference.

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:48.130
Record each source and missing cost.

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:54.547
Do not confuse valued time with actual wages or count the same labor twice.

00:00:54.547 --> 00:00:57.756
This calculation does not establish verified profit.
